hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1714","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' ibn Kuraib, (who said) narrated to us Abu Usamah, from al-A'mash, who narrated to us 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr.\n\nAnd narrated to us 'Ali ibn Khashram, (who said) narrated to us 'Isa.\n\nAnd narrated to us Harun ibn Ishaq, (who said) narrated to us Ibn Fudayl.\n\nAnd narrated to us Salam ibn Junadah, (who said) narrated to us Waki', all of them from al-A'mash.\n\nAnd narrated to us Bundar, (who said) narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Adi, who said: Anba'a us Shu'bah, from Sulayman, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr.\n\nAnd narrated to us Bishr ibn Khalid al-'Askari, (who said) and Akhbarana Muhammad—meaning Ibn Ja'far—from Shu'bah, from Sulayman, who said: I heard 'Umarah narrate from al-Aswad, who said: 'Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud) said:\n\n\None of you should reserve a portion for Shaytan from himself"","" thinking that it is obligatory for him not to turn except to his right. Indeed"","" I have seen the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turn most often to his left.\""\n\n\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
